    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d849">

                <pb facs="0823" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1969</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stimson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-10">September 10,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have examined the British
                    communication of August 21st from Quebec concerning the proposed joint United
                    States-British declaration regarding the Jewish-Arab controversy in Palestine. I
                    regret that the British Foreign Minister and Minister for the Colonies are
                    disappointed in the opinion which I have previously expressed. However, I
                    observe nothing in the British representations to cause a change in my views
                    that there is insufficient military basis for the United States to initiate any
                    action with regards to the situation in Palestine. The War Department will not
                    oppose the action of the State Department on the proposed declaration, but, from
                    the standpoint of the War Department, I am still of the opinion that it is
                    unwarranted.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry L. Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
